.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt ECHO 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm echo
.Nd print arguments separated by spaces
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Join arguments with single spaces and write them to standard output,
followed by a newline.
Only a first argument exactly equal to
.Fl n
suppresses that newline.
Subsequent dash words, including
.Ql -- ,
are literal arguments.
Backslash escapes are not interpreted.
With no arguments print a newline.
.Pp
The shell performs quoting and redirection; the command itself opens no
files and changes no authority.
Use
.Xr printf 1
for formatted output.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after writing and flushing; 1 for output failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo hello world
echo -n label
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr printf 1
